        <h2>How to Access the xAI Grok API</h2>
        <p>
          Follow these steps to get started with the xAI Grok API:
        </p>

        <h3>Step 1: Create an Account</h3>
        <div class="bg-muted/50 p-6 rounded-lg my-8">
          <ol class="space-y-4 text-sm">
            <li><strong>1.</strong> Visit <a href="https://console.x.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">console.x.ai</a></li>
            <li><strong>2.</strong> Sign in with your X (Twitter) account or create a new account</li>
            <li><strong>3.</strong> Complete the developer verification process</li>
            <li><strong>4.</strong> Accept the API Terms of Service</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <h3>Step 2: Generate API Key</h3>
        <div class="bg-muted/50 p-6 rounded-lg my-8">
          <ol class="space-y-4 text-sm">
            <li><strong>1.</strong> Navigate to the API Keys section in your console</li>
            <li><strong>2.</strong> Click "Create New API Key"</li>
            <li><strong>3.</strong> Give your key a descriptive name</li>
            <li><strong>4.</strong> Copy and securely store your API key (it won't be shown again)</li>
          </ol>
          <div class="mt-4 p-4 bg-yellow-100 dark:bg-yellow-900/30 rounded border border-yellow-300 dark:border-yellow-700">
            <p class="text-sm text-yellow-800 dark:text-yellow-200"><strong>Security Note:</strong> Never share your API key or commit it to public repositories. Use environment variables to store keys securely.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Step 3: Make Your First API Call</h3>
        <div class="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 p-6 rounded-lg my-8 overflow-x-auto">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3"># Example API call using curl</p>
          <pre class="text-sm"><code>curl https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -d '{
    "model": "grok-2",
    "messages": [
      {"role": "user", "content": "Explain quantum computing"}
    ]
  }'</code></pre>
        </div>

